  "notes": "22K Derate (TO-2) takeoff V-speeds, both dry and wet runway, transcribed from FCOM PI.30.29 (dry, p.1085) and PI.30.30 (wet, p.1086), 737-800/CFM56-7B26. NOT explicitly itemized in the original 6-file task list (only takeoff_vspeeds_to1.json was requested) -- added because the OPTIMUM thrust-rating selector described in the task cannot evaluate the TO-2 option without its own V-speeds, and this data was already located and transcribed alongside TO-1 from the same FCOM chapter (PI.30). Same nested dry/wet structural shape as takeoff_vspeeds_to1.json. STRUCTURAL DIFFERENCE from TO-1 and from the 26K full-rated tables: the weight axis for TO-2's main V1/VR/V2 table is 80,76,72,68,...,40 (11 points, 4000 kg steps) rather than the 90,85,...,40 (5000 kg steps) axis used by TO-1 and 26K -- TO-2's lower thrust rating caps the tabulated weight range at 80,000 kg. The slope_wind_v1_adjustment weight axis for TO-2 uses all 11 of these same points (matching the main table), unlike TO-1 where the slope/wind table used a coarser 6-point axis -- this is a direct read of the source page layout, not an inference. V1(MCG) is identical between dry and wet, consistent with TO-1 and the 26K tables."
